IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), ss 201A and 201AA (Part 6, Division 1): certain dormant companies exempted from the duty to prepare financial
-- statements, and the retention of the documents laid before the company at its annual general meeting.
-- Whether a company is "dormant" is decided by s 205B(2) and (3) (sgc2's range): taken as an input named for the fact. Whether the company is a listed
-- company, a parent company or a subsidiary company of another corporation is decided in s 4(1) and s 209A: also taken as inputs.
-- The Act's amount of $500,000 (s 201A(5)(a)(ii)(A) and (iii)(A)) may be replaced by the Minister ("such other amount as may be prescribed in substitution"):
-- the functions take the amount as an input, and the constant below is the Act's own figure. A substitution would change the answers of a seat that uses the constant.

DECLARE `s 201A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 201A(7) attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts to the return`
    `s 201AA(1) dispose of the documents within 5 years`

§ `Section 201A(1): the exemption`

-- src:18214 | Certain dormant companies exempted from duty to prepare
-- src:18215 | financial statements
-- src:18217 | 201A.—(1) Subject to subsection (3), the directors of a dormant
-- src:18218 | relevant company are exempt from the requirements of section 201
-- src:18219 | for a financial year if the requirements set out in subsection (2) are
-- src:18220 | satisfied.
@ref s 201A(1) (src:18214-18220)
GIVEN `the company is a relevant company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is dormant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements set out in subsection (2) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice under subsection (3) requiring the directors to comply with section 201 has been issued in time for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201A(1) the directors are exempt from the requirements of section 201 for the financial year` MEANS
    IF    `the company is a relevant company` AND `the company is dormant` AND `the requirements set out in subsection (2) are satisfied`
       AND (NOT `a notice under subsection (3) requiring the directors to comply with section 201 has been issued in time for the financial year`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (3), the directors of a dormant relevant company are exempt from the requirements of section 201 for a financial year if the requirements set out in subsection (2) are satisfied" (a failed "if", and a limit "Subject to subsection (3)": marginal reading (a), NOTES.md; the other reading is NOTHING, since the exemption is grant-like)

§ `Section 201A(2): the requirements for the exemption`

-- src:18224 | (2) The requirements referred to in subsection (1) are —
-- src:18226 | (a) that the relevant company has been dormant —
-- src:18228 | (i) from the time of its formation; or
-- src:18230 | (ii) since the end of the previous financial year;
-- src:18232 | (b) that the directors of the relevant company have lodged with
-- src:18233 | the Registrar a statement by the directors that —
-- src:18235 | (i) the company has been dormant for the period set out
-- src:18236 | in paragraph (a)(i) or (ii), as the case may be;
-- src:18238 | (ii) no notice has been received under subsection (3) in
-- src:18239 | relation to the financial year; and
-- src:18241 | (iii) the accounting and other records required by this Act
-- src:18242 | to be kept by the company have been kept in
-- src:18243 | accordance with section 199; and
-- src:18245 | (c) that the statement mentioned in paragraph (b) has been
-- src:18246 | lodged with the Registrar at the same time that the annual
-- src:18247 | return is required to be lodged under section 197(1).
@ref s 201A(2) (src:18224-18247)
GIVEN `the company has been dormant from the time of its formation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have lodged with the Registrar a statement by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that the company has been dormant for the period set out in paragraph (a)(i) or (ii), as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that no notice has been received under subsection (3) in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that the accounting and other records required by this Act to be kept by the company have been kept in accordance with section 199` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement has been lodged with the Registrar at the same time that the annual return is required to be lodged under section 197(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201A(2) the requirements for the exemption are satisfied` MEANS
    IF    (`the company has been dormant from the time of its formation` OR `the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year`)
       AND `the directors have lodged with the Registrar a statement by the directors`
       AND `the statement says that the company has been dormant for the period set out in paragraph (a)(i) or (ii), as the case may be`
       AND `the statement says that no notice has been received under subsection (3) in relation to the financial year`
       AND `the statement says that the accounting and other records required by this Act to be kept by the company have been kept in accordance with section 199`
       AND `the statement has been lodged with the Registrar at the same time that the annual return is required to be lodged under section 197(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements referred to in subsection (1) are — (a) that the relevant company has been dormant ...; (b) that the directors of the relevant company have lodged with the Registrar a statement by the directors that — (i) ... (ii) ... (iii) ...; and (c) that the statement mentioned in paragraph (b) has been lodged with the Registrar at the same time that the annual return is required to be lodged" (a closed list of requirements)

§ `Section 201A(3): a notice requiring the directors to comply`

-- src:18251 | (3) A relevant person may by written notice require the directors of
-- src:18252 | a dormant relevant company to comply with any or all of the
-- src:18257 | requirements of section 201 in respect of a financial year but the
-- src:18258 | written notice must be issued to the directors not less than 3 months
-- src:18259 | before the end of the financial year.
@ref s 201A(3) (src:18251-18259)
GIVEN `the person is a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice is issued to the directors` IS A DATE
      `the end of the financial year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201A(3) the relevant person may by written notice require the directors of the dormant relevant company to comply with section 201` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a relevant person`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection gives the power to "a relevant person" and is silent on anyone else
    ELSE IF `the notice is in writing` AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the notice is issued to the directors` `the end of the financial year` 3 Months
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may by written notice require ... but the written notice must be issued to the directors not less than 3 months before the end of the financial year" (a proviso that closes the gate: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

§ `Section 201A(4): who is a relevant person`

-- src:18263 | (4) In subsection (3), “relevant person” means —
-- src:18265 | (a) the Registrar;
-- src:18267 | (b) one or more members holding not less than 5% of the total
-- src:18268 | number of issued shares of the company (excluding
-- src:18269 | treasury shares); or
-- src:18271 | (c) not less than 5% of the total number of members of the
-- src:18272 | company (excluding the company itself if it is registered as
-- src:18273 | a member).
@ref s 201A(4) (src:18263-18273)
GIVEN `the person is the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of issued shares of the company held by the member or members who give the notice, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members of the company who give the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of members of the company, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201A(4) the person is a relevant person` MEANS
    IF    `the person is the Registrar`
       OR (`the total number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` GREATER THAN 0
           AND (`the number of issued shares of the company held by the member or members who give the notice, excluding treasury shares` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (`the total number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` TIMES 5))
       OR (`the total number of members of the company, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` GREATER THAN 0
           AND (`the number of members of the company who give the notice` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (`the total number of members of the company, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` TIMES 5))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant person” means — (a) the Registrar; (b) one or more members holding not less than 5% of the total number of issued shares of the company (excluding treasury shares); or (c) not less than 5% of the total number of members of the company (excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member)" (a "means" definition)

§ `Section 201A(5): relevant company, and how dormancy is decided`

-- src:18277 | (5) For the purposes of this section —
-- src:18279 | (a) “relevant company” means a company —
-- src:18281 | (i) which is not a listed company or a subsidiary
-- src:18282 | company of a listed company;
-- src:18284 | (ii) whose total assets at any time during the financial
-- src:18285 | year in question does not exceed —
-- src:18287 | (A) $500,000 in value; or
-- src:18289 | (B) such other amount as may be prescribed in
-- src:18290 | substitution by the Minister; and
-- src:18292 | (iii) which, if it is a parent company (which is not itself a
-- src:18293 | subsidiary company of another corporation), belongs
-- src:18294 | to a group the consolidated total assets of which at
-- src:18295 | any time during the financial year in question does
-- src:18296 | not exceed —
-- src:18298 | (A) $500,000 in value; or
-- src:18300 | (B) such other amount as may be prescribed in
-- src:18301 | substitution by the Minister; and
-- src:18303 | (b) section 205B(2) and (3) applies in determining whether a
-- src:18304 | relevant company is dormant.
@ref s 201A(5) (src:18277-18304)
GIVEN `the company is a listed company or a subsidiary company of a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the highest total assets of the company at any time during the financial year in question, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the company is a parent company which is not itself a subsidiary company of another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the highest consolidated total assets of the group at any time during the financial year in question, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that applies, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201A(5)(a) the company is a relevant company` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `the company is a listed company or a subsidiary company of a listed company`)
       AND `the highest total assets of the company at any time during the financial year in question, in Singapore dollars` AT MOST `the amount that applies, in Singapore dollars`
       AND ((NOT `the company is a parent company which is not itself a subsidiary company of another corporation`)
            OR `the highest consolidated total assets of the group at any time during the financial year in question, in Singapore dollars` AT MOST `the amount that applies, in Singapore dollars`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant company” means a company — (i) which is not a listed company or a subsidiary company of a listed company; (ii) whose total assets at any time during the financial year in question does not exceed — (A) $500,000 in value; or (B) such other amount as may be prescribed ...; and (iii) which, if it is a parent company ..., belongs to a group the consolidated total assets of which ... does not exceed" (a "means" definition)

-- "(A) $500,000 in value" (paragraph (a)(ii) and (iii)); the alternative (B) "such other amount as may be prescribed in substitution by the Minister" is an input of the function above.
@ref s 201A(5)(a) (src:18284-18301)
`s 201A(5)(a)(ii)(A) the amount the section states, in Singapore dollars` MEANS 500000

-- Paragraph (b): section 205B(2) and (3) decide whether a relevant company is dormant. Those subsections are another part's (sgc2): their answer is the input.
@ref s 201A(5)(b) (src:18303-18304)
GIVEN `the company is dormant as section 205B(2) and (3) determine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201A(5)(b) the relevant company is dormant` MEANS
    IF `the company is dormant as section 205B(2) and (3) determine`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "section 205B(2) and (3) applies in determining whether a relevant company is dormant" (the answer is that section's, supplied as a fact: marginal reading, NOTES.md)

§ `Section 201A(6) and (7): financial years that ended before 3 January 2016`

-- src:18311 | (6) This section does not apply to the directors of any company in
-- src:18312 | respect of a financial year which ended before 3 January 2016 and the
-- src:18313 | directors of such company must prepare the accounts or consolidated
-- src:18314 | accounts for that financial year and lay the accounts or consolidated
-- src:18315 | accounts of the company at its annual general meeting for that
-- src:18316 | financial year, in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before
-- src:18317 | that date.
@ref s 201A(6) (src:18311-18317)
GIVEN `the financial year ended on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201A(6) this section applies to the directors for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the financial year ended on` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to the directors of any company in respect of a financial year which ended before 3 January 2016" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only that the section does not apply to a financial year that ended before 3 January 2016; for a later one it says nothing and the rest of the section applies by its own terms

@ref s 201A(6) (src:18311-18317)
GIVEN `the financial year ended on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201A(6) the directors must prepare and lay the accounts under Part VI as it stood` MEANS
    IF `the financial year ended on` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a financial year that ended before 3 January 2016 and is silent on a later one

-- src:18321 | (7) Without limiting section 197(2), a company referred to in
-- src:18322 | subsection (6) must, when lodging a return with the Registrar under
-- src:18323 | section 197, attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts so
-- src:18324 | prepared.
@ref s 201A(7) (src:18321-18324)
GIVEN `the financial year ended on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201A(7) the company must attach a copy of the accounts to the return` MEANS
    IF `the financial year ended on` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company referred to in subsection (6)" is a company with a financial year that ended before 3 January 2016; the subsection is silent on any other

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection ("when lodging a return"): no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 201A(7) (src:18321-18324)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201A act`
`s 201A(7) a company with an old financial year must attach a copy of the accounts to its return` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 201A(7) attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts to the return`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty; dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts to the return" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

§ `Section 201AA(1): keeping the documents laid at the annual general meeting`

DECLARE `s 201AA(2) penalty` HAS
    `s 201AA(2) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 201AA(2) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 201AA(2) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 201AA(2) a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:18328 | Retention of documents laid before company at annual general
-- src:18329 | meeting
-- src:18331 | 201AA.—(1) Every company must cause to be kept at the
-- src:18332 | company’s registered office, or such other place as the directors
-- src:18333 | think fit —
-- src:18335 | (a) a copy of each of the documents that was laid before the
-- src:18336 | company at its annual general meeting under section 201
-- src:18337 | for a period of not less than 5 years after the date of the
-- src:18338 | annual general meeting, being a date on or after 3 January
-- src:18339 | 2016; or
-- src:18341 | (b) in respect of any financial year for which the company
-- src:18342 | need not hold an annual general meeting because of
-- src:18343 | section 175A(1) —
-- src:18345 | (i) a copy of the financial statements; or
-- src:18347 | (ii) in the case of a parent company, a copy of the
-- src:18348 | consolidated financial statements and balance sheet
-- src:18349 | (including every document required by law to be
-- src:18350 | attached thereto),
-- src:18352 | (b) and a copy of the auditors’ report where such financial
-- src:18353 | statements or consolidated financial statements are duly
-- src:18354 | audited, that were sent to all persons entitled to receive
-- src:18355 | notice of general meetings of the company in accordance
-- src:18360 | with section 203(1) for a period of not less than 5 years
-- src:18361 | after the date on which the documents were sent, being a
-- src:18362 | date on or after 3 January 2016.
@ref s 201AA(1) (src:18328-18362)
GIVEN `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year because of section 175A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the annual general meeting at which the documents were laid before the company under section 201` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the documents were sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company in accordance with section 203(1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 201AA(1) the last day of the period for which the company must keep the documents` MEANS
    IF `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year because of section 175A(1)`
    THEN (IF `the date on which the documents were sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company in accordance with section 203(1)` AT LEAST `the day 3 January 2016`
          THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date on which the documents were sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company in accordance with section 203(1)` 5 Years)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) speaks of documents sent "being a date on or after 3 January 2016" and is silent on an earlier date
    ELSE (IF `the date of the annual general meeting at which the documents were laid before the company under section 201` AT LEAST `the day 3 January 2016`
          THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the annual general meeting at which the documents were laid before the company under section 201` 5 Years)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks of an annual general meeting held on "a date on or after 3 January 2016" and is silent on an earlier date

@ref s 201AA(1) (src:18328-18362)
GIVEN `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year because of section 175A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the annual general meeting at which the documents were laid before the company under section 201` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the documents were sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company in accordance with section 203(1)` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201AA(1) the subsection requires the company to keep the documents on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 201AA(1) the last day of the period for which the company must keep the documents` `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year because of section 175A(1)` `the date of the annual general meeting at which the documents were laid before the company under section 201` `the date on which the documents were sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company in accordance with section 203(1)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the date falls before 3 January 2016, which the subsection does not reach
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN IF `the day asked about` AT MOST lastDay
                           THEN JUST TRUE
                           ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not less than 5 years after the date of the annual general meeting" (a period the text fixes in its own words; after it the subsection requires nothing: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

@ref s 201AA(1) (src:18331-18333)
GIVEN `the documents are kept at the registered office of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents are kept at another place that the directors think fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201AA(1) the documents are kept at a place the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the documents are kept at the registered office of the company` OR `the documents are kept at another place that the directors think fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must cause to be kept at the company's registered office, or such other place as the directors think fit" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- "must cause to be kept ... for a period of not less than 5 years after": read as a prohibition on disposing of the documents inside the 5 years (SHANT), as at s 199(2).
@ref s 201AA(1) (src:18328-18362)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days in the 5 years from the date of the annual general meeting or from the date the documents were sent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201A act`
`s 201AA(1) a company must not dispose of the documents within 5 years` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 201AA(1) dispose of the documents within 5 years`
    WITHIN `the number of days in the 5 years from the date of the annual general meeting or from the date the documents were sent`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company disposed of the documents before the end of the 5 years"

§ `Section 201AA(2): the offence of default`

-- src:18366 | (2) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the
-- src:18367 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
-- src:18368 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:18369 | fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:18370 | exceeding 12 months and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 201AA(2) (src:18366-18370)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201AA(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of the offence: the provision's own question; fork F-S1 of NOTES.md)

@ref s 201AA(2) (src:18366-18370)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 201AA(2) penalty`
`s 201AA(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 201AA(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 201AA(2) penalty` OF 5000, 12, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "the offence" the subsection creates; where the person is not guilty of it the subsection fixes no penalty

§ `Section 201AA(3) to (5): the Registrar's power to require a document, and the offences that protect it`

-- src:18374 | (3) The Registrar or an authorised officer may at any time require
-- src:18375 | the company to furnish any document kept under subsection (1), and
-- src:18376 | may, without fee or reward, inspect, make copies of or extracts from
-- src:18377 | such document.
@ref s 201AA(3) (src:18374-18377)
GIVEN `the document is one kept under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person requiring it is the Registrar or an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201AA(3) the company may be required to furnish the document and the document may be inspected` MEANS
    IF `the document is one kept under subsection (1)` AND `the person requiring it is the Registrar or an authorised officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "to furnish any document kept under subsection (1)" and is given to "The Registrar or an authorised officer"; the subsection is silent on any other document or person

-- src:18381 | (4) Any person who —
-- src:18383 | (a) without lawful excuse, refuses to produce any document
-- src:18384 | required of the person by the Registrar or an authorised
-- src:18385 | officer under subsection (3); or
-- src:18387 | (b) assaults, obstructs, hinders or delays the Registrar or the
-- src:18388 | authorised officer in the course of inspecting or making
-- src:18389 | copies or extracts from the document,
-- src:18391 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:18392 | not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:18393 | 2 years or to both.
@ref s 201AA(4) (src:18381-18393)
GIVEN `the person refuses to produce a document required of the person by the Registrar or an authorised officer under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse for refusing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person assaults, obstructs, hinders or delays the Registrar or the authorised officer in the course of inspecting or making copies or extracts from the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201AA(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF (`the person refuses to produce a document required of the person by the Registrar or an authorised officer under subsection (3)` AND (NOT `the person has a lawful excuse for refusing`))
       OR `the person assaults, obstructs, hinders or delays the Registrar or the authorised officer in the course of inspecting or making copies or extracts from the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who — (a) without lawful excuse, refuses to produce any document required of the person ...; or (b) assaults, obstructs, hinders or delays the Registrar or the authorised officer ... shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of the offence: the provision's own question; fork F-S1 of NOTES.md)

@ref s 201AA(4) (src:18381-18393)
GIVEN `the person refuses to produce a document required of the person by the Registrar or an authorised officer under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse for refusing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person assaults, obstructs, hinders or delays the Registrar or the authorised officer in the course of inspecting or making copies or extracts from the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 201AA(2) penalty`
`s 201AA(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 201AA(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person refuses to produce a document required of the person by the Registrar or an authorised officer under subsection (3)` `the person has a lawful excuse for refusing` `the person assaults, obstructs, hinders or delays the Registrar or the authorised officer in the course of inspecting or making copies or extracts from the document` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 201AA(2) penalty` OF 10000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "an offence" under the subsection; where the person is not guilty of it the subsection fixes no penalty

-- src:18397 | (5) In this section, “authorised officer” means an officer of the
-- src:18398 | Authority authorised by the Registrar for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 201AA(5) (src:18397-18398)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised by the Registrar for the purposes of section 201AA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201AA(5) the person is an authorised officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer of the Authority` AND `the person is authorised by the Registrar for the purposes of section 201AA`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“authorised officer” means an officer of the Authority authorised by the Registrar for the purposes of this section" (a "means" definition)
